.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-wallets-tokens-disable - Stop accepting a token on a wallet (soft, reversible)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 wallets tokens disable   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Stop accepting a token on a wallet. The holding is kept, disabled, so
\&'wallets tokens enable' brings it back.  is resolved as for 'enable'.

.PP
Buyers stop being offered this method at once and no new payment can use it;
payments already created with it are unaffected. The wallet's DEFAULT method
cannot be disabled — make another one the default first ('wallets tokens add …
--default').


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--chain-id\fP=0
	Narrow  to one chain when the wallet holds it on several

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for disable

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip the confirmation prompt (required to run non-interactively)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 wallets tokens disable 0xABCD… USDC --chain-id 84532
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-wallets-tokens(1)\fP
